{"data":{"__type":{"kind":"ENUM","name":"AttributeErrorCode","description":"Error codes for attribute operations.","fields":null,"inputFields":null,"interfaces":null,"enumValues":[{"name":"INVALID_ATTRIBUTE","description":"Attribute is invalid - either unknown or not accessible to the requester.\nThese cases are intentionally indistinguishable to prevent leaking attribute names.\nReturned when:\n- Attribute name does not exist in AttributesConfig\n- Attribute exists but requester lacks permission (graphReadable/graphWritable not set or insufficient)\n\nNote: System/downstream errors throw SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE_ERROR instead of using this error code,\nallowing clients to distinguish retriable errors from invalid attribute requests.","isDeprecated":false,"deprecationReason":null},{"name":"INVALID_ATTRIBUTE_VALUE","description":"The provided value failed validation against the attribute's validation rules.\nReturned when the attribute name is valid and accessible, but the value doesn't pass\nthe validation rules configured for that attribute in AttributesConfig.\n\nExamples of validation failures:\n- Text value not in allowed values list\n- Number value outside allowed range\n- List item value doesn't match required pattern\n\nNote: This is different from INVALID_ATTRIBUTE - the attribute itself is valid,\nonly the value is rejected.","isDeprecated":false,"deprecationReason":null},{"name":"LIST_LIMIT_EXCEEDED","description":"Operation would cause the list to exceed the maximum allowed items.\nReturned when adding items to a list attribute would exceed the limit.\nThe operation fails entirely and the list remains unchanged.\nNote: The limit can potentially be relaxed to meet specific requirements.","isDeprecated":false,"deprecationReason":null}],"possibleTypes":null}},"extensions":{"disclaimer":"Public, commercial, and/or non-private use of the IMDb data provided by this API is not allowed. For limited non-commercial use of IMDb data and the associated requirements see ht